{
  "id": "cal",
  "term": "CAL",
  "definition": "CAL refers to the calcarine fissure and surrounding cortex, a brain area measured in this study when examining spontaneous neural activity with resting-state fMRI. In patients with minimal hepatic encephalopathy, activity changes in the right CAL after liver transplantation were linked to changes in cognitive test performance.",
